#
# Counter-example for math:RIngestSourceRetainedConstraint: a math:RIngestRun whose
# math:parseSource witness names its source only BY REFERENCE (math:sourceDigest) and
# never retains it verbatim. An R script is TEXT and is never blob-scale, so the
# by-reference form does not apply to it: a run that cannot show the script it parsed
# never had a parseable script in hand, which is the graph-side residue of the
# front-end's math:MalformedRScript refusal.
#
# The digest is what ISOLATES this rule. The shared math:IngestSourceHeldConstraint is
# satisfied by either form, so a witness holding the digest discharges the general
# hold-your-source obligation and leaves only the R-specific verbatim-retention rule
# firing. The run carries the full grounding frame and produced a codomain, so neither
# math:UngroundedIngestRun nor the native math:UnliftableIngest gate is in play. It fires
# math:RIngestSourceRetainedConstraint (shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent →
# math:MalformedRScript).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/r-ingest-source-not-retained/> .

ex:run a math:RIngestRun ;
    math:parseSource ex:srcWitness ;
    logic:instantiatesSchema ex:schema ;
    logic:instantiatesPlan ex:plan ;
    math:ingestCorrespondence ex:corr .

# Held by reference only — legal for a blob-scale model, wrong for a text script.
ex:srcWitness a math:MathematicalObject ; logic:loadBearing true ;
    math:sourceDigest "b41d8cd98f00b204" .

ex:schema a logic:ActionSchema .
ex:plan a logic:Plan .
ex:corr a logic:Correspondence ;
    logic:morphismClass logic:LossyLens ;
    logic:mnemomorphic true .

ex:lifted a math:MathematicalObject ; gmeow:wasGeneratedBy ex:run .
